Bug: push by name does not parse unparsed files

-olcxpushname has no position, so the include graph cannot say where the name
lives. Like OP_SEARCH and OP_UNUSED_GLOBAL it is project-wide, but it is not in
the "N of M compilation units need reparsing" check in src/server.c, so on a
cold start it answers "No symbol found." With helper.c or other.c parsed first,
the same request finds the definition and all three references.

expected assumes the fix adds OP_BROWSE_PUSH_NAME to that check. The count
(3 of 3) and the wording "before browsing" are guesses; adjust them to what the
fix produces. The goto and reference list are verified.
